        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 532,
        "paragraph_id": "78136433",
        "text": "Damping by vegetation"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 22141,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 625,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 533,
        "paragraph_id": "1AF7F13D",
        "text": "The presence of aquatic vegetation within the area of wave propagation or wave breaking may not only result in short wave dissipation (Section 2.3.2.3), but also in damping of infragravity waves and/or mean flow. Since both long waves and mean flow are fully resolved with the nonlinear shallow water equations, the effect of vegetation can be modeled using a drag force (e.g. Dalrymple et al., 1984), which can be directly added to the momentum equations (Van Rooijen et al., 2015 or see (2.45)):"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 22413,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 629,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 537,
        "paragraph_id": "5331CBAB",
        "text": "Where CD is a drag coefficient, bv is the vegetation stem diameter, N is the vegetation density and u is the wave or current related velocity. To take into account the velocity due to mean flow and infragravity waves, we use the Lagrangian velocity (uL) here. The vegetation-induced time varying drag force is then calculated as the sum of the vegetation-induced drag force per vegetation layer:"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 22532,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 630,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 538,
        "paragraph_id": "385F42DB",
        "text": "(2.53)"
      }
    ],
